# =============================================================================
# Dragon Core / DragonFlight .gitignore
# Everything here is a regenerable BUILD ARTIFACT, not a source-of-truth file.
# Rule of thumb: if scripts/gate.sh (or Yosys/sby/iverilog directly) produces
# it fresh on every run, it's ignored. Docs, specs, packages, generated RTL
# (rtl/*/generated/), and hand-authored RTL (rtl/*/src/) are all tracked --
# they are meaningful state, not run-to-run noise.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Icarus Verilog simulation outputs (simulation/iverilog/) ----
simulation/iverilog/*.vvp
simulation/iverilog/*.log
# (Icarus vvp is a runnable object file, .log is per-run console output --
#  both regenerate every scripts/sim.sh run and have zero value to track.)

# ---- SymbiYosys formal-proof working directories ----
# sby writes a working dir per job run (BMC traces, solver engine state,
# counterexample VCDs). Default naming mirrors the .sby basename with no
# fixed suffix, so this is deliberately broad under verification/formal/.
verification/formal/**/engine_*/
verification/formal/**/*_work/
verification/formal/**/logfile.txt
verification/formal/**/*.vcd

# sby's default top-level output dir is <basename>_<taskname>/, created
# right next to the .sby file for each task it runs (scripts/formal.sh
# invokes sby from within the .sby's own directory). These four suffixes
# are SymbiYosys's standard mode-based task names, so this pattern covers
# any future .sby file's default output directories too, not just this one.
verification/formal/**/*_bmc/
verification/formal/**/*_prove/
verification/formal/**/*_cover/
verification/formal/**/*_live/

# ---- Coverage / regression run artifacts ----
verification/coverage/*
!verification/coverage/.gitkeep
verification/regression/*
!verification/regression/.gitkeep

# ---- Synthesis / bitstream build outputs ----
synthesis/yosys/*
!synthesis/yosys/.gitkeep
synthesis/openlane/*
!synthesis/openlane/.gitkeep
synthesis/reports/*
!synthesis/reports/.gitkeep

# ---- General run-output tree ----
output/logs/*
output/waves/*
output/bitstreams/*
output/netlists/*
output/reports/*
!output/**/.gitkeep

# build_ecp5.ps1 / build_ecp5.sh's disposable working directory --
# wiped and recreated fresh at the start of every build run, never a
# deliverable, never worth tracking.
output/_scratch/

# regenerate.ps1's own hash-marker directory -- confirmed real, appeared
# on disk the first time regenerate.ps1 actually ran. Purely disposable
# staleness-check state (one hash per source document, compared against
# on each run to decide whether to regenerate); never a deliverable, and
# deleting it just forces a full regeneration on the next run rather than
# breaking anything.
tools/.srchash/

# ---- Waveform dumps wherever they land ----
*.vcd
*.fst
*.fst.hier

# ---- Python (pkggen / reggen / check_coverage) ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
tools/**/__pycache__/

# ---- Editor / OS cruft ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- Stale language-server / tooling leftovers ----
# (.slang/ was an orphaned VS Code slang-LSP cache from an earlier toolchain
#  version; guard against it quietly reappearing if an extension regenerates it.)
.slang/

# ---- Local secrets / machine-specific config (should never be committed) ----
.env
*.local

# =============================================================================
# NOTE ON GENERATED RTL (rtl/*/generated/, include/*.sv):
# These ARE tracked deliberately, even though a tool produces them, because:
#   1. CLAUDE.md's hooks treat them as a frozen layer other RTL depends on --
#      they are not regenerated as part of the normal edit/compile/test loop,
#      only when REG/ARCH content actually changes.
#   2. Committing them means anyone (including a future contract designer)
#      can build without first re-running pkggen/reggen against the JSON.
# If you'd rather NOT track generated .sv and instead always regenerate from
# tools/pkggen + tools/reggen at build time, uncomment the two lines below --
# but note CLAUDE.md's skill/hook text currently assumes these files exist on
# disk and would need a "run the generator first" step added to your workflow.
# rtl/*/generated/*.sv
# include/*.sv
